WEBVTT

00:02:57.882 --> 00:03:02.220
I had to smile because, you know,
our dad really loved beer.

00:03:02.553 --> 00:03:06.140
So instead of putting
his ashes in a blasé urn,

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.310
we put them in a big, shiny beer growler.

00:03:09.352 --> 00:03:10.478
(Laughter)

00:03:11.562 --> 00:03:15.483
So my remarks over the growler
were a sincere tribute

00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:17.318
to a superb human being.

00:03:17.902 --> 00:03:20.696
Not unusual as far as eulogies go,

00:03:20.738 --> 00:03:22.573
except for one thing.

00:03:22.615 --> 00:03:24.283
He'd already heard it.

00:03:25.201 --> 00:03:28.246
Those many years earlier,
after I'd received his note

00:03:28.246 --> 00:03:32.250
about how having nice things
said about you while you're alive